@startuml
title RuleSphere - Communication Diagram\n01. Administration | UC-01..04
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor #EDF5FF
skinparam objectBorderColor #496477
skinparam ArrowColor #496477
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 60
object "admin : EnterpriseAdmin" as User <<actor>>
object "api : ManagementAPI" as API <<boundary>>
object "auth : AuthorizationService" as Auth
object "adminService : AdministrationService" as Service
object "resources : ScopedResourceStore" as Store
object "audit : AuditEvidence" as Audit
User --> API : 1: submit(operation, scope)
API --> Auth : 1.1: authorize(principal, operation, scope)
API --> Service : 1.2 [authorized]: apply(operation)
Service --> Store : 1.2.1a [UC-01]: save Tenant/Workspace\n1.2.1b [UC-02]: update scoped roles\n1.2.1c [UC-03]: issue/revoke credential
Service --> Service : 1.2.1d [UC-04]: validate asset and Tenant
Service --> Store : 1.2.2 [UC-04 and valid]: publish immutable library version
Service --> Audit : 1.2.3 [operation succeeded]: append attributable evidence
API ..> User : 1.3: operation result / access or validation error
note bottom of Service
Branches a/b/c/d are alternatives, not consecutive operations.
Invalid assets are not published.
Direct cross-tenant/workspace references are prohibited;
cross-workspace reuse requires a pinned Tenant library.
end note
legend bottom
  Numbered arrows are messages between object roles, not package dependencies.
  1.2 follows 1.1; 1.2.1 is nested in 1.2. [condition] is a guard.
  Routine return messages are omitted; ..> marks the displayed reply.
endlegend
@enduml
